# The physical `L¹ ∩ L²` realization of the scaled radius derivative

The finite-cell correction in the proof of the fractal-dilation theorem is
the actual radius derivative of a dyadic spherical piece.  Multiplying it by
the dyadic cell length produces a family with the same `TT*` normalization as
the undifferentiated family.  This file makes that statement usable by the
finite-shell machinery: its displayed kernel is literally the inverse Fourier
kernel of the scaled derivative pair multiplier, and its physical convolution
agrees almost everywhere with the completed `L²` multiplier on `L¹ ∩ L²`.

